Subject: Loop rotation swaps the fused undefined test instead of inverting it

What this does
  Loop rotation swaps the fused undefined test instead of inverting it.

Why we need it
  `regvm_rotate_loop_test` gives the latch the header test with `REG_CMP_INVERT` flipped.

What it adds
  The rotation swaps the two pseudo tests, which are each other's negation, and inverts only real sub-operations; `tests/differential/corpus/loop-test-undefined-compare.js` covers both senses and operand orders.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 798f1f7..57f93ca 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -62181,7 +62181,14 @@ static void regvm_rotate_loop_test(JSContext *ctx, JSRegIR *ir, int *pc_to_insn,
             continue;
         br->rop = ROP_branch_cmp_reg_reg;
         br->n_ops = 4;
-        br->ops[0] = test->ops[0] ^ REG_CMP_INVERT;
+        /* The latch takes the opposite sense of the header test: REG_CMP_INVERT
+           for a real sub-op; the two pseudo tag tests are each other's
+           negation, so they swap. */
+        if ((unsigned)(test->ops[0] - REG_BIN_IS_UNDEF) < 2)
+            br->ops[0] = test->ops[0] ^
+                         (REG_BIN_IS_UNDEF ^ REG_BIN_IS_NOT_UNDEF);
+        else
+            br->ops[0] = test->ops[0] ^ REG_CMP_INVERT;
         br->ops[1] = test->ops[1];
         br->ops[2] = test->ops[2];
         br->ops[3] = insn_pc[nxt];
